  "english": "Mark 2:13 \"And he went out again\" to verse 22 \"must be put [into fresh wineskins]\".\n\nSaturday. Tone 6 [bki - second side plagal]. Hymn (Ah.): \"Sing to the Lord\".\nPatristic/Resurrection Canticle (Harts), Tone 3 [bdz]: \"Who descended from heaven\". Morning Gospel: Luke 6:1 \"And it came to pass on a sabbath\" to verse 11 \"they might do to Jesus\".\nMidday Liturgy Psalm 40 [41] \"Blessed is he who considers\", [Psalm 41 [42]] \"As pants\", [Psalm 42 [43]] \"Judge me\". Acts 9:1 \"But Saul\" to verse 22 \"this is Christ\".\nCatholic Epistle: 1 Peter 1:13 \"Wherefore, girding up\" to verse 23 \"was preached\". Alleluia, Psalm 65 [66] \"Shout with joy unto God\". Gospel: John 2:12 \"After this he went down\" to verse 22 \"he had said\".\n\nIn the Evening, first Gospel: Matthew 7:1 \"Judge not\" to [Matthew 8:17] \"and bore our sicknesses\". Mesedi: \"Blessed is he who comes\", \"The Lord is our God\". Evening Hymn (Hmb.), Tone 5 [gdz]: \"As you were King\", and also say the other four hymns. Dismissal Gospel: Mark 2:23 \"And it came to pass\" to verse 3:5 \"his hand\".\n\nFifth Sunday [of Easter], which is called World-Church [Red Sunday] (Ashkharhamatran). Tone 7 [dz]: \"Let us bless the Lord\".\nPatristic/Resurrection Canticle (Harts), Tone 7 [dz]: \"We worship\", with its proper verses.\nAnd after the \"Holy God\" [Trisagion], they shall go out with the cross and Gospel in procession, singing the hymn, Tone 7 [dz]: \"Shine, Jerusalem\". Afterward: Psalm 67 [68] \"In the churches bless [God]\", Verse: \"Let God arise\". Proverbs 3:9 \"Honor the Lord\" to verse 17 \"with peace\".\nProphet Isaiah 66:12 \"For thus says [the Lord]\" to verse 16 \"all flesh\".\nEpistle: 1 Timothy 3:14 \"These things I write to you\" to verse 16 \"and taken up in glory\". Alleluia, Psalm 86 [87] \"His foundations\".\nGospel: Matthew 16:13 \"And when Jesus came\" to verse 19 \"loosed in heaven\". And they shall perform the blessing of the fields (Andastan). Litany: \"By this holy cross\". Prayer: \"Keep us [O Christ]\".\nMorning Gospel: Luke 6:12 \"And it came to pass in [those days]\" to verse 49 [Luke 6:49 / 7:11?] \"the ruin of that house was great\".\nSong: \"Newly-created\" [Norasteghtsyal]. Litany: \"Let us ask\". \"Save\". Prayer: \"By your all-powerful\".\nMidday Liturgy Psalm 43 [44] \"We have heard with our ears, O God\", [Psalm 44 [45]] \"My heart overflows\", [Psalm 45 [46]] \"God is our refuge\". Acts 9:23 \"And when [many days] were fulfilled\" to verse 31 \"multiplied\". Psalm 64 [65] \"Praise is due to you\". Catholic Epistle: 1 Peter 2:1 \"Putting away\" to verse 10 \"you have obtained mercy\". Alleluia, Psalm 147 \"Praise [the Lord], O Jerusalem\". Gospel: John 2:23 \"And when he was\" to verse 3:12 \"will you believe?\".\n\nIn the Evening, first Gospel: Matthew 8:18 \"Now when Jesus saw\" to verse 9:8 \"such authority to men\". Mesedi: \"Let your hand be\", \"You who shepherd\". Evening Hymn (Hmb.), Tone 5 [gdz]: \"Co-glorious\", and \"Of the Women\". Dismissal Gospel: Mark 3:6 \"And going out\" to verse 12 \"make him known\".\n\nMonday. Tone 8 [gk]: \"Victorious\".\nPatristic/Resurrection Canticle (Harts), Tone 3 [bdz]: \"Incorruptible\". Morning Gospel: Luke 7:1 \"And it came to pass when\" to verse 10 \"the servant healed\". Midday Liturgy Psalm 46 [47] \"Clap your hands\", [Psalm 47 [48]] \"Great is the Lord\", [Psalm 48 [49]] \"Hear this\". Acts 9:32 \"And it came to pass as Peter went\" to verse 43 \"with a tanner\". Psalm 64 [65] \"Praise is due to you\". Catholic Epistle: 1 Peter 2:11 \"Beloved\" to verse 17 \"honor [everyone]\". Alleluia, Psalm 147 \"Praise [the Lord], O Jerusalem\". Gospel: John 3:13 \"And no one has ascended\" to verse 21 \"are done\".\n\nIn the Evening, first Gospel: Matthew 9:9 \"And passing by from there\" to verse 17 \"both are preserved\". Mesedi: \"The God of gods\", \"From the rising of the sun\". Evening Hymn (Hmb.), Tone 8 [dk]: \"The angel descended\". Dismissal Gospel: Mark 3:13 \"He went up on the mountain\" to verse 19 \"betrayed him\".\n\nTuesday. Tone 1 [adz]: \"Let us sing\". Patristic/Resurrection Canticle (Harts), Tone 3 [bdz]: \"Who are King\". Morning Gospel: Luke 7:11 \"And it came to pass the day after\" to verse 35 \"of her children\". Midday Liturgy Psalm 49 [50] \"The God of gods\", [Psalm 50 [51]] \"Have mercy\", [Psalm 51 [52]] \"Why do you boast\". Acts 10:1 \"There was a certain man in Caesarea\" to verse 23 \"came with him\". Psalm 5:12 \"O Lord, as with a shield\". Catholic Epistle: 1 Peter 2:18 \"Servants, be submissive\" to verse 25 \"of your souls\". Alleluia, Psalm 20 [21] \"The Lord in your strength\". Gospel: John 3:22 \"After this\" to verse 36 \"remains on him\".\n\nIn the Evening, first Gospel: Matthew 9:18 \"While he was [speaking]\" to verse 26 \"all that land\". Mesedi: \"The Lord is powerful\", \"The earth is the Lord's\".",
